-- title:
--   Finite sets of points of the relative Pic⁰ lie in affine opens
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, $C$ a scheme and $c\colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a morphism that is proper, smooth of relative dimension one and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$ over the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, i.e. a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity. Assume that for every $m_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ there is a `FiniteMapData` for $c$ and $\varepsilon$ with invariant $m \ge m_0$: two affine opens $U, V$ with $U \sqcup V = \top$, sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ and a natural number $m$ such that $U$ is exactly the complement of the image of $\varepsilon$, $U \sqcap V$ equals both basic opens $C_f$ and $C_g$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \sqcap V$ are mutually inverse, $\Gamma(C,U)$ and $\Gamma(C,V)$ are finite over $R[X]$ via $f$ and $g$ respectively (for the $R$-algebra structures induced by $c$), and for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s \in S$ the quotient $S \otimes_R \Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$ is a finite free $S$-module of rank $m$. Let $D$ be a `RelativePic0Designation` for $c$, that is a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}\colon D.P \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and a section $D.\mathrm{zeroSection}$ of it, and suppose $D$ represents the subcondition `algEquivZeroCut` of the rigidified relative Picard presheaf of $(c,\varepsilon)$: there is a rigidified line bundle (the Poincaré bundle) on the pullback of $c$ along $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ which is fibrewise algebraically equivalent to zero over all algebraically closed fields, such that for every $t\colon T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and every rigidified line bundle $M$ on the pullback of $c$ along $t$ satisfying the same fibrewise condition there is a unique morphism $T \to D.P$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$ pulling the Poincaré bundle back to a bundle isomorphic to $M$, and the pullback along the zero section is isomorphic to the unit bundle. Assume further that $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth, proper and geometrically connected. Then for every finite set $S$ of points of $D.P$ there is an open subscheme $U$ of $D.P$ which is affine and contains every $x \in S$.
--
--   This is the quasi-projectivity input for the relative Jacobian: the classical statement that a finite set of points of an abelian scheme, or of $\mathrm{Pic}^0_{C/R}$, is contained in an affine open. It is used in the construction of relative Jacobians of smooth proper curves over Noetherian and discrete valuation rings, and in the analysis of the components and $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(p)$.
